1
00:00:30,030 --> 00:01:00,010
See you next time.

2
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:30,010
See you next time.

3
00:01:30,030 --> 00:02:00,010
See you next time.

4
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:04,950
The Tragedy of Ohara.

5
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:07,050
The Terror of the Buster Car.

6
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:12,430
Is that so?

7
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:13,330
Yes.

8
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:14,910
The evidence is clear.

9
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:17,770
This calls for nothing short of the death penalty.

10
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,170
We're waiting for your order.

11
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:20,610
It's unfortunate.

12
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:25,310
Seeing as they've broken the law so blatantly, there's really no other option.

13
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:27,630
We must enforce our own rules.

14
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:30,690
We don't need your mock sympathy, Elder Stars.

15
00:02:30,970 --> 00:02:31,810
Save your breath.

16
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:35,430
You're talking to the leaders of the world, you damn criminal.

17
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:36,790
Show some respect.

18
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:41,650
That must be Professor Clover, Ohara's foremost authority on archaeology.

19
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:44,050
I'm familiar with your work.

20
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:47,130
You've contributed much to the world's cultural heritage.

21
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:50,150
It's sad to see a man of your intellect go astray.

22
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:53,290
The history of this planet belongs to all of mankind.

23
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:59,010
No matter what that history may be, you don't have the right to forbid us from learning it.

24
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:00,610
No one does.

25
00:03:00,990 --> 00:03:01,430
Professor.

26
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:08,550
If one can read the Poneglyphs, then it's also possible that they can revive the ancient weapons and place the world in serious peril.

27
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:14,350
Even if you have the best of intentions, someone else could come along and use your research for evil.

28
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:21,490
Be it good or bad, mankind has the responsibility to accept whatever their history may hold.

29
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:26,550
As long as we don't succumb to fear and ignorance, we will be prepared for anything that may come.

30
00:03:26,690 --> 00:03:27,830
That's idealistic.

31
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:32,270
Is it? Or are you just making convenient excuses to suit your needs?

32
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:36,550
In truth, there are two mysteries left unsolved.

33
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:42,850
Of course we want to read the Poneglyphs, but the reason why they were made in the first place is interesting as well.

34
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:49,290
Why was their message so important that they had to inscribe it on unbreakable stone to pass on to future generations?

35
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:52,750
Why were they hidden and scattered across the world?

36
00:03:53,050 --> 00:03:55,070
Why were they not stored in a library?

37
00:03:55,070 --> 00:04:02,570
The only logical conclusion is that they feared their message would be too easily destroyed if they had written it on paper.

38
00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:05,210
In other words, they had an enemy.

39
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:09,010
Someone who was afraid of the information they wanted to pass on.

40
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:13,890
What are you trying to imply, Professor Clover?

41
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:22,470
Since the ancients have disappeared, we must assume that they were defeated by this enemy, and that whoever they were, they survived through history.

42
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:35,310
It may be no coincidence that roughly 800 years in the past, when the blank century came to an end, the organization we now call the World Government was founded.

43
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:50,470
Therefore, if this unknown enemy was indeed the World Government, it might be in their best interest to erase this inconvenient piece of information and let the ancients disappear into a fabricated blank century.

44
00:04:50,470 --> 00:05:00,190
By analyzing ancient manuscripts and piecing together what we could from the few poneglyphs we were able to find, we discovered the existence of a previously unknown country.

45
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:05,670
Although the details we found were a bit scarce, we believe it was a grand and powerful kingdom.

46
00:05:05,670 --> 00:05:12,310
And yet, despite their strength, not a trace remains, or rather, those traces were deliberately erased.

47
00:05:12,570 --> 00:05:16,910
But they were prepared for this possibility, even as they faced the threat of extinction.

48
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:24,970
And so they etched their history in stone, before their kingdom was crushed under the might of the Allied Nations, now known as the World Government.

49
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:28,990
Thus, the reason why the poneglyphs were made becomes quite clear.

50
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:32,770
I see. That's a bold hypothesis.

51
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:36,310
It's true that the ancient weapons would be a threat to the world.

52
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:43,310
But more so than weapons, what I believe the World Government is afraid of is the history surrounding this lost kingdom.

53
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:48,290
Its existence and its ideologies are so dangerous to you that you would kill to keep them secret.

54
00:05:49,410 --> 00:05:53,730
Although we still don't know what makes you fear this kingdom, we do at least know its name.

55
00:05:54,050 --> 00:05:58,090
Since we've gone so far already, perhaps you'd like me to share it with you now.

56
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:04,490
Kill him!

57
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:15,530
Professor!

58
00:06:19,530 --> 00:06:21,810
You left us no choice.

59
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:26,950
How dare you!

60
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:28,390
No, Professor!

61
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:31,110
Ohara knows too much.

62
00:06:33,610 --> 00:06:35,850
You may give the order to attack.

63
00:06:36,090 --> 00:06:37,670
Or don't move an inch!

64
00:06:37,810 --> 00:06:38,230
No!

65
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,670
You mustn't let anyone escape!

66
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:53,530
Now then, with a golden transponder snail entrusted to me by Admiral Sengoku...

67
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:54,030
Professor!

68
00:06:54,890 --> 00:06:55,450
Robin!

69
00:06:56,210 --> 00:06:57,370
You fool!

70
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:58,870
I told you to run!

71
00:06:59,290 --> 00:06:59,610
Hurry!

72
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,910
I invoked the buster call!

73
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:04,030
And that's a wrap!

74
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:06,170
He pressed something!

75
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:07,290
What is that?

76
00:07:07,290 --> 00:07:10,010
Get out of here!

77
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:10,530
Go!

78
00:07:11,210 --> 00:07:11,770
No!

79
00:07:11,990 --> 00:07:13,370
I don't want to be alone!

80
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:15,250
You have to stop being so selfish!

81
00:07:15,910 --> 00:07:17,170
This isn't the time!

82
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:19,290
Robin!

83
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:24,950
It's the buster call!

84
00:07:25,450 --> 00:07:27,210
All battleships to your positions!

85
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:28,510
Prepare to open fire!

86
00:07:28,510 --> 00:07:28,670
Fire!

87
00:07:31,210 --> 00:07:31,770
What?

88
00:07:32,630 --> 00:07:33,190
Hey!

89
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:33,870
Look!

90
00:07:34,810 --> 00:07:37,090
The Tree of Knowledge is on fire!

91
00:07:37,610 --> 00:07:38,090
Dammit!

92
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:39,170
What are you doing?

93
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:40,250
Are you insane?

94
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,430
Isn't it enough to take our lives?

95
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:45,050
Hey, it's not my fault.

96
00:07:45,290 --> 00:07:47,570
Must have caught fire when they bombed your secret basement.

97
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:50,590
Stop this!

98
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:51,370
Right now!

99
00:07:51,570 --> 00:07:53,430
You can't replace the documents in there!

100
00:07:53,530 --> 00:07:54,250
Don't you realize that?

101
00:07:54,250 --> 00:07:54,470
You!

102
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:55,310
Don't move!

103
00:07:55,690 --> 00:07:56,030
Whoa!

104
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:58,270
We don't need guns anymore.

105
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:01,670
Time for the government agents to pull out.

106
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:04,590
Protect the books!

107
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:07,990
Let's put out the fire!

108
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:08,470
Hurry!

109
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:20,670
Pass the water over here!

110
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,430
Carry as many books outside as you can!

111
00:08:25,430 --> 00:08:41,030
Bring that woman with you.

112
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,050
Get up!

113
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:47,110
There's still some info we have to wring out of her.

114
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:48,350
She can't die yet.

115
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:50,670
Just make sure she doesn't escape again.

116
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:52,010
acompañ in there!

117
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:55,790
Mami!

118
00:08:57,430 --> 00:08:58,050
Please, Robin,

119
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:03,550
run while you still can.

120
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:05,650
You can't die here.

121
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:06,550
Not like this.

122
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:08,450
Mami, no!

123
00:09:08,450 --> 00:09:16,450
Go! We're done for. There's no point in staying.

124
00:09:20,450 --> 00:09:21,450
Robin!

125
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:22,450
Robin, don't!

126
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:33,450
You're my mother, aren't you?

127
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:42,450
Make up your mind, Olvia. Are you going to board this ship or not?

128
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:44,450
Mommy!

129
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:47,450
I'm holding her back! Just hurry and get on!

130
00:09:47,450 --> 00:09:52,450
Mommy! Mommy! No! Mommy!

131
00:09:52,450 --> 00:09:57,450
I'm sorry, Robin. I can never call myself your mother again.

132
00:09:57,450 --> 00:10:02,450
After all these years, after all I've done, I don't have the right anymore.

133
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:12,450
Monster!

134
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,450
Monster!

135
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:16,450
She's so scary! Her mom ran away!

136
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:19,450
Hey! That's my daughter's dress! You take it off!

137
00:10:19,450 --> 00:10:22,450
I'm sorry, Aunt Roji. I just wanted to try it on.

138
00:10:22,450 --> 00:10:24,450
You sure eat a lot for a freeloader.

139
00:10:24,450 --> 00:10:35,450
Please answer me!

140
00:10:37,450 --> 00:10:39,450
Are you my mom?

141
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:48,450
Hold on. That girl your daughter or what?

142
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:51,450
No.

143
00:10:52,450 --> 00:10:53,450
Olvia!

144
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:55,450
I'm sorry, little girl.

145
00:10:56,450 --> 00:11:00,450
You must be confusing me with someone else.

146
00:11:01,450 --> 00:11:05,450
Even if it comes to this, I don't want you to be the daughter of a criminal.

147
00:11:06,450 --> 00:11:07,450
Olvia!

148
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:09,450
Huh. What a weird little brat.

149
00:11:10,450 --> 00:11:11,450
Right. Let's go.

150
00:11:21,450 --> 00:11:26,450
It's me! It's Robin!

151
00:11:27,450 --> 00:11:28,450
It's me! It's Robin!

152
00:11:29,450 --> 00:11:31,450
I've grown since the last time!

153
00:11:31,450 --> 00:11:33,450
So maybe you don't recognize me!

154
00:11:34,450 --> 00:11:36,450
I've been waiting for you all these years!

155
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:38,450
Are you sure?

156
00:11:39,450 --> 00:11:40,450
You're really...

157
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:44,450
Not my mom!

158
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:45,450
Help me!

159
00:11:45,450 --> 00:11:46,450
Just once!

160
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:48,450
Someday...

161
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:50,450
I wanted to hold your hand...

162
00:11:51,450 --> 00:11:53,450
And walk together like a family!

163
00:11:54,450 --> 00:11:55,450
I studied hard!

164
00:11:55,450 --> 00:11:56,450
To become an archaeologist!

165
00:11:57,450 --> 00:11:58,450
So I could go to sea with you!

166
00:11:58,450 --> 00:12:00,450
I could read the Pornoglyphs too!

167
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:04,450
What did she say?

168
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:05,450
Robin! No!

169
00:12:06,450 --> 00:12:08,450
So please, look at me!

170
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:10,450
Let me stay with you!

171
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:12,450
Mom!

172
00:12:13,450 --> 00:12:14,450
Robin!

173
00:12:16,450 --> 00:12:17,450
I've waited so long!

174
00:12:18,450 --> 00:12:19,450
We're finally together!

175
00:12:20,450 --> 00:12:22,450
Don't leave me alone again!

176
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,450
Moon again!

177
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:46,450
Oh no! Now what's going on?

178
00:12:47,450 --> 00:12:48,450
Now commencing the buster call.

179
00:12:49,450 --> 00:12:50,450
All ships fire at once.

180
00:12:50,450 --> 00:12:53,450
Everything on the island of Ohara is your target.

181
00:12:53,450 --> 00:12:54,450
Let nothing remain!

182
00:12:55,450 --> 00:12:59,450
The research conducted here was far more extensive than we anticipated.

183
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:01,450
Make sure that knowledge is not passed on.

184
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:03,450
Do not allow it to leave the island.

185
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,450
Annihilate the devils of Ohara!

186
00:13:07,450 --> 00:13:08,450
Turn it to the ground!

187
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:10,450
In the name of justice!

188
00:13:14,450 --> 00:13:15,450
Damn it!

189
00:13:15,450 --> 00:13:16,450
What the hell?

190
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:18,450
Can't you wait till we leave the island?

191
00:13:18,450 --> 00:13:19,450
They're gonna kill us!

192
00:13:20,450 --> 00:13:21,450
Stop it!

193
00:13:22,450 --> 00:13:24,450
The Tree of Knowledge took a direct hit!

194
00:13:25,450 --> 00:13:27,450
They're using their highest power against us.

195
00:13:27,450 --> 00:13:30,450
They staged their investigation, but they were planning this from the start.

196
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:32,450
Bastards!

197
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:33,450
Hey, Chief.

198
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:34,450
That girl said she can read the Poneglyps.

199
00:13:35,450 --> 00:13:36,450
Yeah.

200
00:13:36,450 --> 00:13:37,450
She did, didn't she?

201
00:13:37,450 --> 00:13:38,450
I don't know if it's true or not, though.

202
00:13:39,450 --> 00:13:41,450
Probably safer to wipe her out just in case.

203
00:13:41,450 --> 00:13:42,450
Don't let her leave the island.

204
00:13:43,450 --> 00:13:44,450
Remember her face, alright?

205
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:46,450
We're retreating.

206
00:13:47,450 --> 00:13:48,450
Then I'll grab Olvia.

207
00:13:49,450 --> 00:13:50,450
Screw it!

208
00:13:51,450 --> 00:13:52,450
The situation has changed!

209
00:13:52,450 --> 00:13:53,450
Just run!

210
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:55,450
I'm not gonna get blown up trying to follow some stupid order!

211
00:13:56,450 --> 00:13:58,450
Our number one priority is keeping me alive!

212
00:13:58,450 --> 00:13:59,450
Retreat!

213
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:01,450
Everyone back to the ship!

214
00:14:09,450 --> 00:14:11,450
Put out the fire on that side before it spreads!

215
00:14:12,450 --> 00:14:14,450
Protect the library at all costs!

216
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:37,450
I've been waiting a long time to do this!

217
00:14:40,450 --> 00:14:41,450
I'm glad!

218
00:14:45,450 --> 00:14:46,450
Robin!

219
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:50,450
Mommy!

220
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:55,450
Robin, forgive me.

221
00:14:55,450 --> 00:14:56,450
Please!

222
00:14:57,450 --> 00:15:00,450
This is my fault for not watching over you with more care!

223
00:15:01,450 --> 00:15:04,450
Is it really true that you can read the Poneglyphs?

224
00:15:05,450 --> 00:15:09,450
I had to learn, since I wanted to be a scholar!

225
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:11,450
I never knew my little girl was an archaeologist.

226
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:13,450
That's amazing!

227
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:15,450
You must have studied hard while I was gone, huh?

228
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:18,450
These aren't things that just anyone can do.

229
00:15:19,450 --> 00:15:20,450
I'm so proud!

230
00:15:20,450 --> 00:15:31,450
Fortunately, the only ones who know about this are the officials who were here earlier.

231
00:15:32,450 --> 00:15:33,450
We can't afford to waste any more time!

232
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:35,450
Olvia!

233
00:15:35,450 --> 00:15:36,450
Take Robin and run!

234
00:15:37,450 --> 00:15:41,450
If you can sneak her onto the evacuation ship, she might still be able to leave the island!

235
00:15:45,450 --> 00:15:46,450
Robin!

236
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:48,450
I've been looking all over for you!

237
00:15:48,450 --> 00:15:49,450
It's Saul!

238
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:51,450
So you met with your mother after all!

239
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:53,450
Saul!

240
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:54,450
Why in the world are you here?

241
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:56,450
Guess it must be fate!

242
00:15:57,450 --> 00:16:00,450
I just happened to wash up here, and your little girl was the one who found me!

243
00:16:01,450 --> 00:16:02,450
Anyhow, we ain't got time to chat right now!

244
00:16:03,450 --> 00:16:04,450
You gotta get off this island!

245
00:16:05,450 --> 00:16:08,450
I'll be fine, but I need you to take care of Robin for me, please!

246
00:16:09,450 --> 00:16:12,450
But why? What about you? Are you going to come with me?

247
00:16:12,450 --> 00:16:13,450
Are you going to come with me?

248
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:15,450
Olvia, are you?

249
00:16:16,450 --> 00:16:18,450
I can't leave yet. There's something left to do.

250
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:20,450
No, Mom! You can't leave me now!

251
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:24,450
I'll stay here with you! I don't want to lose you again!

252
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:29,450
Robin, if you're a scholar of Ohara, you should know that history is mankind's greatest treasure.

253
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:33,450
Now that it's been passed on, it will illuminate the path to your future.

254
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:39,450
However, you must pass it on as well, or its light will disappear with the next generation.

255
00:16:40,450 --> 00:16:42,450
Share those books! I'll take these!

256
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:45,450
We weren't trying to uncover some dark secrets.

257
00:16:46,450 --> 00:16:49,450
We simply wanted to hear the voices of the past and protect them.

258
00:16:50,450 --> 00:16:55,450
Unfortunately, our research ends here, but time marches on, even if Ohara is destroyed.

259
00:16:56,450 --> 00:17:01,450
And as surely as we believe in the past, we believe in the future that you will inherit.

260
00:17:01,450 --> 00:17:04,450
What does that mean?

261
00:17:05,450 --> 00:17:08,450
Someday, you'll know.

262
00:17:09,450 --> 00:17:14,450
Hurry! Take her and go, Saul!

263
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:17,450
Are you sure?

264
00:17:18,450 --> 00:17:19,450
Yeah.

265
